---
import AsterLayout from "../../layouts/AsterLayout.astro";
import { ASTER_DEX_ID, AUTHORS, PERSON_ID, SITE_URL } from "../../entity";
import { buildAsterPageGraph, buildBreadcrumbs } from "../../lib/schema";
import { ASTER_DOCS, ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED } from "../../data/aster";

const url = `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/hidden-orders/`;
const description =
  "Aster hidden orders and hidden positions: how they stay out of the public book, how they differ from iceberg orders and dark pools, and where privacy ends.";

const articleNode = {
  "@type": "TechArticle",
  "@id": `${url}#article`,
  headline: "Hidden orders",
  alternativeHeadline: "Hidden orders and hidden positions on Aster",
  name: "Hidden orders and hidden positions on Aster",
  description,
  url,
  mainEntityOfPage: url,
  inLanguage: "en",
  datePublished: "2026-11-24",
  dateModified: ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED,
  author: { "@id": AUTHORS.kirsty.id },
  editor: { "@id": AUTHORS.maksim.id },
  publisher: { "@id": PERSON_ID },
  isPartOf: { "@id": `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/#collection` },
  articleSection: "Trading",
  about: [
    { "@id": ASTER_DEX_ID },
    { "@type": "Thing", name: "Order book" },
    { "@type": "Thing", name: "Dark pool" },
  ],
  citation: [
    { "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "Hidden order and hidden position", url: `${ASTER_DOCS}trading/perpetuals/order-types/hidden-order-and-hidden-position` },
    { "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "Privacy overview", url: `${ASTER_DOCS}aster-chain/overview` },
  ],
};

const breadcrumbs = buildBreadcrumbs(`${url}#breadcrumbs`, [
  { name: "Home", url: `${SITE_URL}/` },
  { name: "Aster DEX", url: `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/` },
  { name: "Hidden orders", url },
]);

const graph = buildAsterPageGraph([articleNode, breadcrumbs]);
---

<AsterLayout
  title="Aster Hidden Orders and Hidden Positions Explained | Maksim Sokal"
  description={description}
  canonical={url}
  graph={graph}
  trail={[{ label: "Hidden orders" }]}
  modified={new Date(ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED)}
>
  <header class="space-y-5 max-w-3xl">
    <span class="text-xs font-mono text-sky-400 uppercase tracking-widest block">Trading</span>
    <h1 class="font-display font-medium text-3xl md:text-4xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight leading-tight">
      Hidden orders
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      A hidden order is a limit order that never appears in the public book. The position it creates is also excluded
      from public feeds and portfolio analytics. It is the most direct expression of Aster's privacy thesis, and it has
      specific limits.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-400">
      Verified <time datetime={ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}>{ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}</time> ·{" "}
      <a href={`${ASTER_DOCS}trading/perpetuals/order-types/hidden-order-and-hidden-position`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">official docs</a>
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="what-heading">
    <h2 id="what-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">What is hidden</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">The order</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          No size, price or presence appears on the public order book. It still shares liquidity with visible orders, so
          it can fill against normal flow.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">The position</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          The resulting position is excluded from public data feeds and portfolio analytics. Size, direction and PnL are
          visible to you, not to outside observers.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
      Hidden orders are limit orders only. Matching, margin and liquidation operate on the full position size; privacy
      changes visibility, not the risk engine.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="compare-heading">
    <h2 id="compare-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">How it differs from similar tools</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-[#1e293b]/60">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-brand-950/60 border-b border-[#1e293b]/40">
            <th scope="col" class="text-left text-[10px] text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-widest px-5 py-3 font-semibold">Property</th>
            <th scope="col" class="text-left text-[10px] text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-widest px-5 py-3 font-semibold">Hidden order</th>
            <th scope="col" class="text-left text-[10px] text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-widest px-5 py-3 font-semibold">Iceberg</th>
            <th scope="col" class="text-left text-[10px] text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-widest px-5 py-3 font-semibold">Dark pool</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#1e293b]/30">
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-xs text-slate-300">Invisible to the book</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-xs text-emerald-300">Yes</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-xs text-slate-400">Partially</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-xs text-emerald-300">Yes</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#1e293b]/30">
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-xs text-slate-300">Minimal market impact</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-xs text-emerald-300">Yes</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-xs text-slate-400">No</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-xs text-emerald-300">Yes</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-xs text-slate-300">Access to public liquidity</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-xs text-emerald-300">Yes</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-xs text-emerald-300">Yes</td>
            <td class="px-5 py-3 text-xs text-rose-300">No</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
    <h2 id="how-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Placing one</h2>
    <ol class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed list-decimal pl-5">
      <li>Open Aster Perps (Pro mode), choose the contract, leverage and amount.</li>
      <li>Tick the <strong>Hidden Order</strong> checkbox. It becomes a limit order automatically.</li>
      <li>The order appears under Open Orders with a not-visible icon, but not in the public book.</li>
      <li>Once filled, the position appears in your Positions tab and remains private to your account.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6" aria-labelledby="limits-heading">
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <h2 id="limits-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-lg text-slate-100 tracking-tight">What it solves</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <li>Position hunting: your liquidation level is not advertised.</li>
        <li>Copy trading: observers cannot mirror the order before it fills.</li>
        <li>Market impact: large orders do not signal intent to the book.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="font-display font-medium text-lg text-slate-100 tracking-tight">What it does not solve</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <li>Liquidation risk. The risk engine still closes the position at the mark price.</li>
        <li>Fill risk. A hidden limit order may never fill.</li>
        <li>Deposit visibility. The source-chain transfer remains public.</li>
        <li>Your own disclosure. A viewer pass can reveal history.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-[#1e293b]/60 pt-6 space-y-2">
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Related: <a href="/aster-dex/privacy/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">privacy mechanics</a> ·
      <a href="/aster-dex/liquidation-risk/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">liquidation risk</a> ·
      <a href="/aster-dex/fees/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">fees</a>
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Written by <a href="/kirsty-moreland/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Kirsty Moreland</a> · Technical review by{" "}
      <a href="/about/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Maksim Sokal</a> ·
      <a href="/disclosure/" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-sky-300">Disclosure</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</AsterLayout>
